# Where the painter puts a border and a shadow, in four pictures a person can
# read. Each one is a rule CSS states and the painter used to get wrong, and
# each was a bug of its own:
#
#   * **A border is inside the box** (buri#76). `edges-border-widths.png` is
#     five boxes, one to a width, all thirty tall with their top edge at y=20.
#     Every width is that many solid rows starting at y=20, the odd ones
#     included — a one-pixel border used to straddle the edge and paint two
#     half-covered rows, one of them above the box.
#   * **A border with no colour is the foreground** (buri#88).
#     `edges-current-colour.png` is three boxes: one whose `Foreground` is the
#     only colour it has, one told a colour of its own, and one taking the
#     foreground it inherited. Only the middle one is red; the others are the
#     colour their text would be. They used to be black.
#   * **An outer shadow is outside the box** (buri#90).
#     `edges-focus-ring.png` is the same spread-only ring on a transparent box
#     and on a white one. Both rings are three pixels wide and the transparent
#     box still shows the page behind it — the ring used to fill the control.
#   * **…whatever its blur and offset** (buri#90 again).
#     `edges-lift.png` is Tailwind's `shadow-xs` — a pixel down, two of blur,
#     no spread — on a transparent box over a red page, the same box with no
#     shadow at all, and the same lift at half black so the hairline can be
#     seen. Read across any of the three at their middle and the two hundred
#     pixels between x=20 and x=219 are the page: the lift is the fringe
#     outside them. A ring is only the loudest shape of the rule, and the
#     blurred, offset one is what a design system actually ships.
#
# The negative twin moves the foreground of the first box in the second
# picture. That is the row's whole claim: a border with no colour follows the
# foreground, so exactly that picture fails.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs. Textproto,
# but not a Buri file: only repo/ below is a Buri repository.

doc: "a border of every width inside its box, a border taking the foreground it was given, and a ring and a blurred lift outside the box that cast them"

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/edges", "--force"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "pass.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/edges/test/__snapshots__/edges-border-widths.diff.png"  exists: false }
path { path: "lib/edges/test/__snapshots__/edges-current-colour.diff.png"  exists: false }
path { path: "lib/edges/test/__snapshots__/edges-focus-ring.diff.png"  exists: false }
path { path: "lib/edges/test/__snapshots__/edges-lift.diff.png"  exists: false }

edit {
  file: "lib/edges/edges.buri"
  replace: ".Foreground(.Rgb(18, 18, 28)),"
  with: ".Foreground(.Rgb(214, 44, 44)),"
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/edges", "--force"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "changed.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/edges/test/__snapshots__/edges-current-colour.diff.png"  exists: true }
path { path: "lib/edges/test/__snapshots__/edges-border-widths.diff.png"  exists: false }
path { path: "lib/edges/test/__snapshots__/edges-focus-ring.diff.png"  exists: false }
path { path: "lib/edges/test/__snapshots__/edges-lift.diff.png"  exists: false }
